@startuml analyse-parcours-p2
title Web journey analysis workflow — Page 2/5 : DISPATCH + EcoIndex

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  BorderColor #5BA1BC
  FontColor #1C2856
}
skinparam actor {
  BackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  BorderColor #5BA1BC
  FontColor #1C2856
}
skinparam ArrowColor #5BA1BC
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #5BA1BC
skinparam SequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #ECECF2
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #5BA1BC
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #E0F0F4
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9BD0DD
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "User" as U #82C1DD
participant "Claude\n(skill analyse-parcours)" as C #82C1DD
participant "Sub-agents\n(HAR / Coverage)" as SA #C8E6C9
participant "analyze_har.py" as AH #DBDDE5
participant "Measurement scripts\n(har_metrics.py, CWV)" as EI #DBDDE5
database "audit-dir/" as FS #9BD0DD

== Step 25 — DISPATCH capability detection ==

C -> C : Sub-agents available?\n(Claude Code -> YES, others -> sequential)

== Wave 1 — HAR + Coverage analysis (in parallel) ==

par
  C -> SA : :::dispatch analyze-har\n(20_har-analysis.md)
  SA -> AH : python3 analyze_har.py <source-dir>
  AH -> AH : Traffic + performance (requests, domains,\nHTTP codes, duplicates, blocking resources)
  AH -> FS : har-analysis.json
else
  C -> SA : :::dispatch analyze-coverage\n(30_coverage-analysis.md)
  SA -> FS : Read Coverage-*.json
  SA -> SA : Detect format A or B
  SA -> SA : JS/CSS metrics per page\n(total, unused, %)
  SA -> SA : Multi-page summary + outliers
  SA -> FS : coverage-analysis.json
end

note over C, SA
  Platform mode:
  Claude Code -> native sub-agents (isolated context windows)
  Other platforms -> sequential inline execution
  Disk result identical in both cases
end note

== Merge Wave 1 ==

C -> FS : Read har-analysis.json
FS -> C : Network traffic data
C -> FS : Read coverage-analysis.json
FS -> C : Dead JS/CSS code data

== Step 35 — EcoIndex calculation (main context) ==

C -> EI : python3 har_metrics.py <har> [cwv.json]
EI -> EI : Extract HTML DOM from\nresponse.content.text
EI -> EI : Count requests + weight\nper page (pageref)
EI -> C : Table: score/grade/req/KB/DOM\nper page + onLoad

note over C, EI
  Limits:
  - DOM=0 if HAR without HTML body
    (response.content.text absent)
  - SPA: DOM = initial state only
    (not after JS hydration)
  These cases are documented in the report.
end note

== Step 37 — Core Web Vitals ==

alt cwv.json already present
  C -> C : CWV collection skipped
else GOOGLE_API_KEY available (priority path)
  C -> EI : python3 collect_cwv_pagespeed.py <audit-dir>
  EI -> EI : PageSpeed Insights API\n(CrUX field + Lighthouse lab, per page)
  EI -> FS : cwv.json\n{lcp, inp, cls, source: "pagespeed/crux"}
  FS -> C : cwv.json ready
else GOOGLE_API_KEY absent (fallback)
  C -> C : Extract URLs from HAR\n(log.pages[].title)
  C -> EI : run_lighthouse.sh <audit-dir> <url1> <url2> ...
  EI -> EI : Lighthouse CLI (npx or local install)\nper page in lab mode
  EI -> FS : cwv.json\n{lcp, inp, cls, source: "lighthouse"}
  FS -> C : cwv.json ready
else No source available
  C -> C : Warning: report without CWV\n(HAR onLoad used as LCP proxy)
end

@enduml
